<title>GERMANY: Audi CEO expects higher 1996 sales.</title>
<headline>Audi CEO expects higher 1996 sales.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Audi AG chief executive officer Herbert Demel said he expected the German luxury carmaker to report higher 1996 sales but for unit sales to be below 500,000 units.</p>
<p>Demel, in comments to the Stuttgart press club late on Thursday, said the carmaker, a division of Volkswagen AG, expected further growth in 1997 and to top unit production of 500,000. Audi in 1995 produced 448,200 units.</p>
<p>Demel also said he expected Audi to have a German market share of of over six percent. The carmaker had a domestic market share of 6.2 percent in 1995.</p>
</text>
